## STATE MANAGEMENT (Observation Framework)
- Use `@Observable final class` for ViewModels (never ObservableObject or @Published).
- Pass `let viewModel: MyViewModel` to child views (no @StateObject).
- Use `@Bindable` for two-way bindings.
- `@State` only for pure local UI state.
- `@Environment` for app-wide state.
- All UI-updating code must be annotated `@MainActor`.
- Prefer value types (structs) over classes unless identity or reference semantics are required.
- Use async/await + Task for concurrency.